      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J%C3%B3zsefv%C3%A1ros"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Neo‑Baroque Eurostars Palazzo Zichy, built in 1899 for Count Nándor Zichy, now houses a luxury hotel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitcity.travel/en/budapest/district/jozsefvaros"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pál utca, Mária utca and Füvészkert, the botanical garden, are the real locations where Ferenc Molnár’s classic novel The Paul Street Boys was set.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J%C3%B3zsefv%C3%A1ros"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Józsefváros once housed brick factories around Gutenberg tér and Rákóczi tér, reflecting its industrial past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
